	abstract = {Modern enterprise applications are built using distributed, data-intensive microservice architectures and lack formal verification frameworks for proving the correctness of these applications. We propose a new verification approach that integrates enterprise-grade applications with object-centric process mining. In our approach, event logs from our applications are used to mine object-centric Petri nets. The mined Petri nets are then analyzed using the GreatSPN tool [2] to verify liveness and safety properties. We conducted experiments on simulated event data to demonstrate that high-quality models can be automatically mined and used for formal verification. Our framework enables scalable and automated analysis of complex microservice systems, advancing formal methods in data-intensive distributed architectures. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
