	abstract = {Enterprise architecture framework has become the key computing infrastructure of digital transformation, which provides systematic abstraction mechanism and automatic coordination ability. This paper introduces a rigorous method to design digital enterprise architecture based on TOGAF framework, with emphasis on algorithm efficiency, distributed computing paradigm and formal modeling technology. The implementation includes service-oriented architecture (SOA) with micro-service decomposition, event-driven message queue with Apache Kafka (50 partitions, replication factor 3), and container arrangement with horizontal automatic expansion function through Kubernetes. The digital architecture integrates real-time ETL pipeline with O(n log n) complexity, distributed storage system and multi-layer caching strategy using Redis cluster. The technical infrastructure has deployed a hybrid cloud architecture that combines private cloud security with public cloud resilience, while API Gateway (Kong 3.0) uses token bucket algorithm to achieve a rate limit of 10,000 requests per second. Through database index (B+ trees), connection pool (HikariCP) and asynchronous processing (Celery with MQ), the performance has been optimized, and the average API response time has been reduced from 850 milliseconds to 120 milliseconds (a decrease of 85.9%), the system throughput has increased from 1,200 transactions per second to 8,500 transactions (an increase of 608%), and the overall system availability has reached 99. The architecture adopts circuit breaker mode, distributed tracking (Jaeger), service grid (Istio) and canary deployment strategy with automatic rollback mechanism. The paired t test (p < 0.001) was used for statistical verification, and it was confirmed that all 42 evaluation business processes were significantly optimized. This computing framework based on TOGAF shows how systematic application of computer science principles, including algorithm design, data structure optimization and distributed system theory, can promote the digital transformation of power industry. © 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Architecture governance; Business structure; Enterprise architecture; TOGAF; Top design},
